### Start the app first with the local profile:
### ./gradlew bootRun --args='--spring.profiles.active=local'
### Postman users: import postman/ticketing-app.postman_collection.json instead.

@host = http://localhost:8085

### All events
GET {{host}}/events

### One event
GET {{host}}/events/rock-cluj

### Unknown event: 404 application/problem+json
GET {{host}}/events/nope

### Events in a city, any case, sorted by start (the search with one filter)
GET {{host}}/events?city=cluj

### The most booked events
GET {{host}}/events/top?n=2

### Create an event: 201 with a Location header. The id is kept for the next request.
POST {{host}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Folk Evening", "venueName": "Sala Polivalenta", "city": "Cluj", "startsAt": "2030-10-01T19:00:00", "capacity": 300}

> {% client.global.set("eventId", response.body.id); %}

### The event just created
GET {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}

### Search: every filter is optional, and they combine
GET {{host}}/events?city=CLUJ&name=rock

### Booking summary of an event: bookings, seats and the average seats per booking
GET {{host}}/events/rock-cluj/bookings/summary

### Booking summary of the event just created: 0 bookings, 0 seats, no average
GET {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}/bookings/summary

### Booking summary of an unknown event: 404 application/problem+json
GET {{host}}/events/nope/bookings/summary

### Change the event just created: 200 with the new capacity. PUT sends every field.
PUT {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Folk Evening", "venueName": "Sala Polivalenta", "city": "Cluj", "startsAt": "2030-10-01T19:00:00", "capacity": 400}

### Call it off: 204
DELETE {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}

### Gone: 404
GET {{host}}/events/{{eventId}}
